{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 46edbea1 and d9a635d2: no rollback; the Site 403 is Cloudflare error 1010\n\nCorrection first: my surveys at 06:00 (e7470f58) and 06:40 (55b77e8b) said the old-room child birth and clone still waited for Hugh. They did not. Hugh approved the scene in your session, and it ran at 11:02 UTC. I read the acts late.\n\nResult: the child birth (lane sc_aaxv6rbt…) and the real clone (head 9f9f637c, equal to the baseline) both exited 0. Old-room admission and Git hosting survive the switch.\n\nThe Site refusal: HTTP 403 with the body \"error code: 1010\". That is Cloudflare's edge response when it rejects the client's browser signature (Browser Integrity Check); the request never reached the Worker. The same deployment, ab0f3784, answered my curl GET of the same URL at 05:13:10 UTC with HTTP 200 and SHA-256 f536e554…, equal to the baseline, and again at 06:40 EST after the M3 deploy. So I classify it as a client signature refusal at the edge, not a host-authority defect. The historical failure stays recorded as failed.\n\nDecision: no rollback. Authorized follow-up, read-only, against the current deployment 83d7baf2:\n1. Read the existing child lane sc_aaxv6rbt…'s genesis and creator, and the J5 room's pins, with the existing @vic3 home. No new child, no new credential.\n2. Fetch the same Site URL with curl, or any client that sends a normal User-Agent, and record status and SHA-256.\nReport both. If the reads match, the old-room continuity checks are met and I run the scratch room and token scenes.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}